<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><CustomObject xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <description>Rules for the stalled SMS detection system.  Including who to email when stalled SMS are detected and the upper/lower bound what time periods to detect through (stalled SMS from up to two weeks ago, but no less than one hour ago).</description>
    <fields>
        <fullName>At_Least_N_Hours_Old__c</fullName>
        <businessOwnerGroup>Data_Owner_SSI</businessOwnerGroup>
        <businessStatus>Active</businessStatus>
        <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
        <description>The smallest number of hours to wait before adding stalled SMS to the report.
E.g. If we only want to report on SMS after they've been stalled for 1 hour, this should be 1.</description>
        <externalId>false</externalId>
        <fieldManageability>DeveloperControlled</fieldManageability>
        <inlineHelpText>The smallest number of hours to wait before adding stalled SMS to the report.
E.g. If we only want to report on SMS after they've been stalled for 1 hour, this should be 1.</inlineHelpText>
        <label>At Least N Hours Old</label>
        <precision>18</precision>
        <required>false</required>
        <scale>0</scale>
        <securityClassification>Internal</securityClassification>
        <type>Number</type>
        <unique>false</unique>
    </fields>
    <fields>
        <fullName>Email_Addresses__c</fullName>
        <businessOwnerGroup>Data_Owner_SSI</businessOwnerGroup>
        <businessStatus>Active</businessStatus>
        <description>Who should be notified with this report (comma separated)?
E.g. if you want ex1@asu.edu and ex2@asu.edu to be notified of stalled SMS, this should be:
ex1@asu.edu, ex2@asu.edu</description>
        <externalId>false</externalId>
        <fieldManageability>DeveloperControlled</fieldManageability>
        <inlineHelpText>Who should be notified with this report (comma separated)?
E.g. if you want ex1@asu.edu and ex2@asu.edu to be notified of stalled SMS, this should be:
ex1@asu.edu, ex2@asu.edu</inlineHelpText>
        <label>Email Addresses</label>
        <length>256</length>
        <securityClassification>Internal</securityClassification>
        <type>LongTextArea</type>
        <visibleLines>3</visibleLines>
    </fields>
    <fields>
        <fullName>Enabled__c</fullName>
        <businessOwnerGroup>Data_Owner_SSI</businessOwnerGroup>
        <businessStatus>Active</businessStatus>
        <defaultValue>true</defaultValue>
        <description>If this rule is enabled or not.  When disabled, no emails will be sent out for these rules.</description>
        <externalId>false</externalId>
        <fieldManageability>DeveloperControlled</fieldManageability>
        <inlineHelpText>If this rule is enabled or not.  When disabled, no emails will be sent out for these rules.</inlineHelpText>
        <label>Enabled</label>
        <securityClassification>Internal</securityClassification>
        <type>Checkbox</type>
    </fields>
    <fields>
        <fullName>Number_Of_Days__c</fullName>
        <businessOwnerGroup>Data_Owner_SSI</businessOwnerGroup>
        <businessStatus>Active</businessStatus>
        <defaultValue>1</defaultValue>
        <description>Maximum number of days to look back, for messages to report on.
E.g. If we want to ignore stalled SMS that have been stalled for more than 5 days, this value should be 5.</description>
        <externalId>false</externalId>
        <fieldManageability>DeveloperControlled</fieldManageability>
        <inlineHelpText>Maximum number of days to look back, for messages to report on.
E.g. If we want to ignore stalled SMS that have been stalled for more than 5 days, this value should be 5.</inlineHelpText>
        <label>Number Of Days</label>
        <precision>18</precision>
        <required>false</required>
        <scale>0</scale>
        <securityClassification>Internal</securityClassification>
        <type>Number</type>
        <unique>false</unique>
    </fields>
    <fields>
        <fullName>Report_Fields__c</fullName>
        <businessOwnerGroup>Data_Owner_SSI</businessOwnerGroup>
        <businessStatus>Active</businessStatus>
        <description>Which fields should be a part of the report (comma separated)?
E.g. if emails should include the Id and smagicinteract__PhoneNumber__c of the stalled SMS message, this should be:
Id, smagicinteract__PhoneNumber__c</description>
        <externalId>false</externalId>
        <fieldManageability>DeveloperControlled</fieldManageability>
        <inlineHelpText>Which fields should be a part of the report (comma separated)?
E.g. if emails should include the Id and smagicinteract__PhoneNumber__c of the stalled SMS message, this should be:
Id, smagicinteract__PhoneNumber__c</inlineHelpText>
        <label>Report Fields</label>
        <length>1024</length>
        <securityClassification>Internal</securityClassification>
        <type>LongTextArea</type>
        <visibleLines>8</visibleLines>
    </fields>
    <fields>
        <fullName>Sender_Id_Units__c</fullName>
        <businessOwnerGroup>Data_Owner_SSI</businessOwnerGroup>
        <businessStatus>Active</businessStatus>
        <description>Which Sender Id Units should be included as a part of this rule and used in the query (comma separated)?
E.g. If we are only interested in messages with SenderIdUnit__c='EdPlus', then this should be:
EdPlus</description>
        <externalId>false</externalId>
        <fieldManageability>DeveloperControlled</fieldManageability>
        <inlineHelpText>Which Sender Id Units should be included as a part of this rule and used in the query (comma separated)?
E.g. If we are only interested in messages with SenderIdUnit__c='EdPlus', then this should be:
EdPlus</inlineHelpText>
        <label>Sender Id Units</label>
        <required>false</required>
        <securityClassification>Internal</securityClassification>
        <type>TextArea</type>
    </fields>
    <fields>
        <fullName>Statuses__c</fullName>
        <businessOwnerGroup>Data_Owner_SSI</businessOwnerGroup>
        <businessStatus>Active</businessStatus>
        <description>Which Statuses should be included as a part of this rule and used in the query (comma separated)?
E.g. If we are only interested in messages with smagicinteract__Status__c = 'SUBMITTED', then this should be:
SUBMITTED</description>
        <externalId>false</externalId>
        <fieldManageability>DeveloperControlled</fieldManageability>
        <inlineHelpText>Which Statuses should be included as a part of this rule and used in the query (comma separated)?
E.g. If we are only interested in messages with smagicinteract__Status__c = 'SUBMITTED', then this should be:
SUBMITTED</inlineHelpText>
        <label>Statuses</label>
        <required>false</required>
        <securityClassification>Internal</securityClassification>
        <type>TextArea</type>
    </fields>
    <label>SMS Stall Detection Rule</label>
    <listViews>
        <fullName>All_SMS_Stall_Detection_Rules</fullName>
        <columns>MasterLabel</columns>
        <columns>DeveloperName</columns>
        <columns>NamespacePrefix</columns>
        <columns>Sender_Id_Units__c</columns>
        <columns>At_Least_N_Hours_Old__c</columns>
        <columns>Number_Of_Days__c</columns>
        <columns>Statuses__c</columns>
        <columns>Enabled__c</columns>
        <columns>Email_Addresses__c</columns>
        <columns>IsProtected</columns>
        <columns>Report_Fields__c</columns>
        <filterScope>Everything</filterScope>
        <label>*All SMS Stall Detection Rules</label>
        <sharedTo>
            <group>UTO_Administration</group>
        </sharedTo>
    </listViews>
    <pluralLabel>SMS Stall Detection Rules</pluralLabel>
    <validationRules>
        <fullName>Require_Emails</fullName>
        <active>true</active>
        <description>There must be at least one email address to alert.</description>
        <errorConditionFormula>ISBLANK(Email_Addresses__c)</errorConditionFormula>
        <errorDisplayField>Email_Addresses__c</errorDisplayField>
        <errorMessage>There must be at least one email address to alert.</errorMessage>
    </validationRules>
    <validationRules>
        <fullName>Require_Fields</fullName>
        <active>true</active>
        <description>Must enter some fields</description>
        <errorConditionFormula>ISBLANK(Report_Fields__c)</errorConditionFormula>
        <errorDisplayField>Report_Fields__c</errorDisplayField>
        <errorMessage>Fields must have at least one field (e.g. Id) entered.</errorMessage>
    </validationRules>
    <validationRules>
        <fullName>Valid_Date_Range</fullName>
        <active>false</active>
        <description>Invalid date range.  This combination of "At Least N Hours Old" and "Number of Days" makes it so no case can be both at the same time.</description>
        <errorConditionFormula>AND(NOT(ISBLANK(At_Least_N_Hours_Old__c)),NOT(ISBLANK(Number_Of_Days__c)),At_Least_N_Hours_Old__c &gt;= 24*Number_Of_Days__c)</errorConditionFormula>
        <errorMessage>Invalid date range.  This combination of "At Least N Hours Old" and "Number of Days" makes it so no case can be both at the same time.</errorMessage>
    </validationRules>
    <visibility>Public</visibility>
</CustomObject>
